  "id": "control-experiment",
  "term": "control experiment",
  "definition": "A control experiment is a test set up in conditions where the supposed cause cannot be acting, to see whether the expected effect still appears. It serves as a check on conclusions drawn from other experiments by helping separate the effect from the presumed cause.",
